#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059713 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059526 :question/id #uuid "0adf8fad-9a6f-5eb1-970f-11633ba98ca1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4295" :question/problem "The vectors $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are given in the picture below. Find the coordinates of $\\vec{a}+6\\vec{b}$.\n\n![](images/56/56b10e759084da6fb21c8421bc9ff6d74aac2602df28f6c8e478bd874d7d6e9f.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^(→) + 6b^(→) &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc55e44b-82d0-5145-8a24-d43bc60dc594" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815c3a41-9158-597c-a900-28f71dc19e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3, 5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056527} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c16558-0f65-5213-8725-6982d8f91873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056528} {:answer/id #uuid "2632c7be-399a-59a9-a1c5-d3040176c2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056529} {:answer/id #uuid "3630aa01-0ede-53a0-9581-47ac3d27e799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056530} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7a8a07-59eb-509a-98b9-cc938456eba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056531}] :answer-field/id #uuid "09d60f5c-a8df-5e06-be54-94be00ab60af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056526